  "heat": 2,
  "text": "One woman said no to her husband. The empire passed a law about it. Esther chapter one. A king with one hundred and twenty-seven provinces throws a seven day party. Royal wine. Whole city invited. Day seven, direct quote: \"the heart of the king was merry with wine.\" Cute. So he sends seven men to fetch his wife. Bring Queen Vashti out in the royal crown, let the people and the princes look at her beauty. Meanwhile Vashti is hosting her own feast. For the women. Same palace. Same week. She says no. That is the entire receipt. Scripture records the refusal and not one syllable about why. Anybody telling you her reasons is writing fanfiction. Does he go and talk to his wife? Absolutely not. He convenes a legal panel. \"What shall we do unto the queen Vashti according to law?\" Enter Memucan. And I am not exaggerating what he says. This is not just about you, king. If word gets out, every woman in the empire hears it, and they will start despising their husbands. So they write it into the law of the Persians and the Medes. The kind that cannot be repealed. Vashti never comes before the king again. And letters go out to every province, in every language: every man shall bear rule in his own house. One woman said no at a dinner party. And an entire empire had to legislate.",
